WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:04.100
- [Peter] I just really miss him.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.360
- I don't think Tony
would've done what he did,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.910
if he didn't know that
you were gonna be here

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:08.806
after he was gone.

00:00:08.806 --> 00:00:11.556
(dramatic music)

00:00:17.074 --> 00:00:18.370
- You gonna be the next Iron Man now?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.290
- [Peter] Well no, I don't have time,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.604
I'm too busy doing your job.

00:00:20.604 --> 00:00:21.437
(cops groan)
- What?

00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:23.610
- I'm kidding, I'm kidding,
look, keep up the good work,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.110
because I am going on vacation.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.810
- [Naz] First of all
congratulations, guys,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.161
Because the movie is amazing.

00:00:30.161 --> 00:00:30.994
- Thanks.
- Thank you so much.

00:00:30.994 --> 00:00:32.770
- [Naz] And I feel like
I'm finally recovering

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.338
from Infinity War, like
after watching this movie.

00:00:35.338 --> 00:00:36.171
- [Jacob] Nice.

00:00:36.171 --> 00:00:39.010
- And for me, Spider-Man's
dusting was actually

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.370
the hardest to watch,
but I'm curious to know,

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.640
what were your personal reactions

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.313
to seeing Spider-Man get dusted?

00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:47.153
- It was sad.
- You probably laughed.

00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:49.960
- I was laughing, I was
laughing in the movie theater,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.500
straight up and then like
especially in Endgame,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.420
when everyone was dying,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.640
that was hilarious.
- [Tom] Just cracking up.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.697
- Super funny, like the
part where he's like,

00:00:57.697 --> 00:00:59.957
"We won Mr. Stark, we won."

00:01:01.181 --> 00:01:03.053
- You're dark, man.

00:01:03.053 --> 00:01:04.480
- Good stuff, guys.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.280
- I thought, yeah, I was very emotional,

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.393
but I thought, I was emotional
about the whole situation,

00:01:09.393 --> 00:01:12.543
but also a little worried about my job.

00:01:13.512 --> 00:01:14.660
I was like--
- So we're dead?

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.163
- So we're still on for a while, right?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.490
- Because I could've
sworn this was something

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:20.440
we were supposed to do.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:24.610
- Yeah, but he's coming back, right?

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.160
- From your lawyer, like oh no.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.260
- Tom, for you, what was your reaction

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.680
when you found out Spider-Man
was gonna get dusted?

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.130
- It was actually the same exact reaction.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.567
I was like "That's really
cool, right, but I come back?

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.580
"Right, I'm not actually dying?"

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.000
It was pretty much the same reaction.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.303
- Like I still have a job?

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.650
What I love about this movie too

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.090
is that you really feel
like Iron Man's ghost

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.810
or spirit truly lives on,

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.860
but what were your guys'
reactions when Iron Man died?

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.580
- I mean, everybody's
like heartbroken again.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.850
- It was pretty tough,
it was pretty tough,

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.510
'cause we've all grown up
with Robert playing Iron Man

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.860
and he's such an iconic character.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.760
Everyone's looked up to him

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.300
and I think you could argue

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.420
that his character's had the
most incredible character arc

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.593
from Iron Man One to Endgame
maybe in cinematic history.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.940
We said goodbye to someone who we all love

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.080
and we will miss him and
this film is kind of like

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.620
a token of our love to what
Robert Downey Jr. created

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.920
and Jon Favreau, when he
made those first two films.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.200
So yeah, so it's a really nice kind

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.428
of love note to Iron Man.

00:02:26.428 --> 00:02:27.270
- You've got to remind yourself

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.926
that Robert Downey Jr. is still alive.

00:02:28.926 --> 00:02:30.360
- Yeah, he's still good.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.200
- He is still there, you know.
- He's still thriving.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.890
- The real guy is still there.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.099
- I agree, sometimes we forget.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:38.599
- [Tom] Yeah, that is so true.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.280
- He had such an incredible run, you know?

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.490
Like over a decade.
- [Tom] Amazing.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:44.730
- It's just a legacy.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.850
But going off that theme though,

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.940
Tom, I'm curious to know how long

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.970
do you want to play Spider-Man?

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.420
- I honestly would play Spider-Man

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.290
until like I can't walk anymore.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.710
I love this character so much,

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.743
and it was like my childhood
dream to play this character.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.110
I'm loving it, I'm really enjoying it.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.190
I'm really loving what
we can do with this movie

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.330
and the people that we can kind of touch

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.610
and the amazing things we're
able to do with the platform

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.450
that this movie gives us.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.030
So yeah, I'm just really enjoying it.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.130
- I do want to ask you Tom

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.840
about your bromance with Jack Gyllenhaal,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.350
because I know you've
done so many interviews,

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:21.290
even before you were
Spider-Man about how much

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.910
and how badly you wanted
to work with Jake,

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.600
so what was that like finally?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.750
- I mean, it was amazing.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.510
It's always a scary thing in the industry

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.170
when you meet someone that you look up to

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.460
because you want them to
live up to your expectations

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.803
and Jake did that and then some.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.780
He's such a great actor

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.070
and he's someone I've really admired,

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.363
so working with him was kind
of like a bit of a masterclass.

00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:43.700
It was just kind of crazy how we became

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.393
such good friends so quickly.

00:03:47.571 --> 00:03:49.300
I look forward to working
with him again in the future,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.050
whether it's in a Spider-Man movie

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.610
or whether it's in a
small little Indie movie

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.170
where we, I don't know,
play brothers or something.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.570
But yeah, I'm just really, really glad

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.700
that he is everything I
would have hoped he would be

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.060
and then some.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.230
- Are the rumors true that it
was hard to get through scenes

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.980
because you guys were just
laughing the entire time?

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.350
- Yeah, totally true.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.100
Sometimes just laughing at nothing.

00:04:10.168 --> 00:04:11.560
There's a scene in the
film where we shake hands

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.760
for the first time and
there was nothing funny

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.129
about the scene at all,
but we just couldn't

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:18.430
get it in.
- Stop laughing.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.480
That's always a thing though,

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.490
like when you're not supposed to laugh,

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.520
that's when you can't stop laughing.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.353
- Exactly.
- And then they're like,

00:04:22.353 --> 00:04:23.991
"Okay, now we need you
to laugh at the scene."

00:04:23.991 --> 00:04:24.879
- You're tired or something.
- You're like,

00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:26.730
"I don't want to laugh."

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.170
- I don't.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.030
- Not finding this funny.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.636
They're just kind of like...

00:04:31.636 --> 00:04:32.800
(dramatic music)

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.363
- [Mysterio] What do you want Peter?

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:36.550
- I want to go back on my trip

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.417
with the girl who I really like

00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:38.820
and tell her how I feel.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.653
MJ, I--

00:04:39.653 --> 00:04:40.653
- Am Spider-Man?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.270
- [Peter] No, of course I'm not...

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.403
- I mean it's kind of obvious.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.750
- You're right, you may not be ready,

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.690
but this is my responsibility.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.843
Saving the world requires sacrifice.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.767
Sometimes people die.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.823
(explosion)

00:04:56.823 --> 00:04:57.800
- Oh my God.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.746
- [Naz] First of all,
congratulations on this film.

00:04:59.746 --> 00:05:00.579
- Thank you.

00:05:00.579 --> 00:05:02.930
- It was so exhilarating and exciting

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.300
to see you in a Spider-Man movie.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.060
I was so excited.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.770
There's something somewhat seamless

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.480
about you coming into this universe

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.730
and playing a character named Mysterio,

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.680
given some of your past roles.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.020
I want to know did any of
your smaller Indie roles

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.870
inform or influence
your role in this movie?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.470
- Every role you play informs
the experience of a role

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.420
and how you play it and all this stuff,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.650
but yeah, there were...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.900
The themes of this movie are,

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:35.820
some of them are somewhat
similar to other movies I've done

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.780
so I was familiar kind of with that play,

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.390
particularly like the
idea of a rift in time

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.620
and coming to another space

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.700
and a different time and continuums,

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.980
time continuums and things like that.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.540
So I was somewhat familiar
with what that was

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.430
and the behavior that happens in that.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.243
I've done a number of
movies about that idea.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.560
Then I think what Peter
goes through in this movie

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.970
is similar to some things that
characters I've been through

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.310
in movies have gone through.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:10.010
So I could empathize with
what he was going through.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.800
I've also obviously grown
up and am older than him,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.090
so because of the character Mysterio,

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:20.971
I could impart wisdom that
I had learned in a way

00:06:20.971 --> 00:06:23.480
through playing parts
that went through things

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.210
like he goes through in this movie.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.043
Does that make sense?

00:06:26.043 --> 00:06:27.460
- Totally, and I'm sure it helps

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.310
that you've had training
or acting under a bubble

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.750
or a fish bowl in the past.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.793
- Yes, absolutely.

00:06:35.355 --> 00:06:37.470
I've done a lot of acting in small spaces,

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.610
partially suffocated, so yes, yes.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.420
- I want to dive deeper into Mysterio

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.690
just because he's so iconic.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.670
He was in issue 13 of Spider-Man.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.840
Throughout the years we've
seen four different versions

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.460
of him and he's typically
portrayed as a villain.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:53.680
So as much as you can tell me,

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.093
how different is your Mysterio
from comic book Mysterio?

00:06:57.093 --> 00:06:59.560
- I mean, that's what I
loved about what Marvel did

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.890
when they came to me with
the idea of this character.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:07.890
Which was that he's very
different from the comics.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.320
Because, yes, he appears early
on in the Spider-Man comics,

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.180
he's an important part and
he's very an important part

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.290
in the comics to Peter
Parker and to Spider-Man.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:23.290
But he's also not as iconic
as some other characters

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.920
in the comics.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.740
So it allows you some
leeway and I like that,

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.140
'cause we could change
some behavior and we did.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.433
That gave me an opportunity
to add some things

00:07:35.433 --> 00:07:38.500
that I think probably
wouldn't have been there,

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.360
if you had to stay strict to the scripture

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:46.360
of roles like Spider-Man
or things like that.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.300
- I love just how they connect
your character into the MCU.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.480
I can't wait for people to
find out how that goes down.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:53.530
It's awesome.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.490
I was just talking to
Tom and he was telling me

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.630
that sometimes you guys would
just be shooting a scene

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.460
and laughing about nothing,

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.740
something that wasn't even funny.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.140
Tell me about this
bromance you have with Tom.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.815
- It's a romance.

00:08:05.815 --> 00:08:07.290
I'm really sick of people
calling it a bromance,

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.220
it's a romance, it's a legitimate romance.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.930
I find that to be very uncomfortable
when you see two people

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.270
of the same sex really falling in love.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.350
He's a wonderful person.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.300
He's devoted to his work, which I love.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.500
He's obsessed with
learning about the craft,

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.563
which I love too.

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:30.380
He could be someone in his
position who has a big ego

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.226
and kind of walks in with a knowledge,

00:08:33.226 --> 00:08:37.160
even at that age though, you
have all your insecurities,

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.710
as we all do, and he's just not like that.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:40.720
He's very honest.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.960
He admits to those things.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.767
He wants to listen.

00:08:43.767 --> 00:08:45.660
I really love the way he works.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.110
So when we first started working together,

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.470
he's also very gracious and very like...

00:08:50.358 --> 00:08:53.530
He's really knows how
to make me feel special

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:55.170
and tells me that he
thinks I'm a great actor

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:56.963
so that obviously goes a long way.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.190
He's just a good dude and we
actually enjoy each other,

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.940
which a lot of people
talking in press junkets

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.160
about other actors say,

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.100
but this is true.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.300
It's true.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.990
- If you were to play Mysterio again,

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.560
would you rather play him

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.370
with Spider-Man, Wolverine, or Deadpool?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:22.523
- Well you can cross Deadpool
out right off the bat.

00:09:24.117 --> 00:09:27.610
I have so much deep respect for Wolverine

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.467
and same for Spider-Man
so I can't really say.

00:09:34.633 --> 00:09:36.636
- I always feel like I'm
putting my friends in danger.

00:09:36.636 --> 00:09:37.469
(girl screams)

00:09:37.469 --> 00:09:39.095
The world needs the next Iron Man.

00:09:39.095 --> 00:09:41.843
(dramatic music)

00:09:41.843 --> 00:09:43.833
- Are you going to step up or not?

00:09:43.833 --> 00:09:46.098
(monster roars)

00:09:46.098 --> 00:09:49.548
(dramatic music)

00:09:49.548 --> 00:09:52.320
- [Naz] It's so good to
see you, congratulations.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.153
- Thank you.

00:09:53.153 --> 00:09:56.770
- On your 11th film in the
MCU and playing Nick Fury.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.120
It's been so awesome
just watching Nick Fury's

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.010
kind of evolution.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.850
In this movie, I wanted
to talk to you about

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.840
kind of this new journey and new identity

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.560
that Nick Fury is on right now.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.610
There's no more S.H.I.E.L.D.,
who is he working for?

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.130
What's going on?

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.060
- Well he's still working for S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:19.060
and there's still an Avengers Initiative.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:22.430
It's just trying to
figure out what's happened

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:27.820
in the blip time and what
his new normal has to be.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.240
He knows what his directive

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:33.013
from Tony Stark was about Peter.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.410
He's kind of like that
uncle or grandfather

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.307
who's trying to say,
"When you gonna grow up?

00:10:39.307 --> 00:10:40.417
"Take responsibility.

00:10:40.417 --> 00:10:41.357
"They tell me you're the guy,

00:10:41.357 --> 00:10:44.180
"but you're not showing
that you're the guy."

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.080
He's saying, "Just let me
be a teenager for a while."

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.327
He said, "No, you don't
have time to do that.

00:10:49.327 --> 00:10:51.597
"The world is not going
to wait on you to grow up,

00:10:51.597 --> 00:10:52.930
"so you gotta grow up quick."

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:55.620
So I'm kind of that pestering relative.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.880
- Yes, and I love Nick Fury

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.465
because he also just kind of
keeps the Avengers together.

00:11:01.465 --> 00:11:02.337
- [Samuel] Tries to.

00:11:02.337 --> 00:11:03.170
- He tries to.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.850
He's the glue that
keeps them all together.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:09.490
I want to know if Nick
Fury was never snapped,

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:13.740
what would he have done
in the Endgame events?

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:14.723
- Well what he did.

00:11:16.191 --> 00:11:17.760
He knew what he had to do

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.630
and he had just enough
time to get it done.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.450
He would've been around to
see what Carol was going to do

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.520
and probably who have gotten in her way

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.400
or tried to tell her another
way to do what she was doing.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.540
- Obviously you've been in 11 films.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.400
Is there a memorable Nick Fury moment

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.730
that stands out to you?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.100
- Well, the beginning.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.050
The first one, when I step out
of the dark in Tony's house.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.787
The "You are Iron Man",

00:11:43.787 --> 00:11:47.040
"I am Iron Man" moment
which is kind of cool,

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.757
made everyone kind of sit up and go,

00:11:48.757 --> 00:11:50.720
"Oh my God, this is gonna be awesome."

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.440
That's number one.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:57.350
And watching what happened with Carol

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:00.810
and when Nick realized
there were other people

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:04.250
in the universe that
needed to be dealt with

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:07.450
and the threat was just as viable

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:10.390
from out there as it was from down here,

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:14.110
and being able to learn
that and watch him grow

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.990
in terms of being a naive government agent

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.930
into the careful and crazy and

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.043
kind of paranoid Nick Fury that he is.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.440
- I really loved the Nick
Fury and Captain Marvel

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:28.390
'cause I feel like him and Carol have this

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.050
kind of father-daughter relationship.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.020
But you see this softer side of Nick

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.096
where he's singing Hey Mr. Postman.

00:12:35.096 --> 00:12:36.250
- No, stop.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:38.203
- [Naz] That's my favorite Nick Fury.

00:12:39.573 --> 00:12:41.970
- I'm putting out an
oldies album next month.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:42.803
- [Naz] I would love to hear it.

00:12:42.803 --> 00:12:44.040
- Nick Fury sings the oldies.

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.960
- I would love to hear it.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:48.520
I'm curious though for you how long

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.240
do you want to play Nick Fury for?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.580
Because after watching this movie,

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.270
I'm excited that he's still a presence.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.690
I want to see him go far into Phase Four.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.405
How long do you see
yourself playing Nick Fury?

00:12:58.405 --> 00:13:00.540
- I don't know, I haven't
given any thought.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.530
I guess as long as I can
physically embody him

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:08.530
and make him believable
and viable in a way.

00:13:09.841 --> 00:13:12.560
I don't want to overstep my time,

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.870
whatever that is.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.870
- [Naz] No, I don't think
that could ever be possible.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.730
- No, Marvel will let me know,

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:19.810
I'm pretty sure.

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:22.560
(exciting music)

